  user_input {
    user_response: "User prompt: Act as an expert Full-Stack Developer and UI/UX Designer. Build a fully functional, highly modern, and animated Event Landing Page for a \"Chess eSports\" tournament.\n\nTech Stack: Use HTML, CSS, JavaScript (or React with Tailwind CSS depending on the tool capability).\n\nKey Requirements & Features:\n\n1. Modern Dark UI/UX Design (eSports Vibe):\n\nUse a sleek, premium dark mode aesthetic (Deep slate background #0f172a, with glowing accents like neon violet #8b5cf6 and gold #fbbf24 to match the flyer).\n\nUse crisp glassmorphism effects for content cards (schedules, rules, awards) rather than flat, boring boxes.\n\nTypography should be bold, modern, and highly legible, suited for a competitive gaming event.\n\n2. Core Website Sections (Based on the Event Flyer):\n\nHero Section: Big, bold title: \"CHESS eSPORTS: Compete. Think. Conquer.\" Display the key stats prominently: \"2 Days | 100 Players | 1 Champion\" alongside a glowing \"Register Now\" Call-to-Action button.\n\nAbout & eSports Experience: A grid section highlighting event features: Global Vibes, Live Boards, Live Commentary, and Audience Engagement. Use modern icons for each.\n\nTournament Overview & Format Details: A visual flowchart or clean step-layout showing the progression. Day 1 (100 Players -> Swiss System 5 Rounds -> Top 32 Qualify -> Round of 32). Day 2 (Round of 16 down to Grand Final). Include a small tooltip or text block explaining the Knockout rules (Best of 3, Best of 5, Blitz/Armageddon Tie-breaks).\n\nInteractive Schedule: An interactive Tab or Accordion component allowing the user to switch seamlessly between \"Day 1 Schedule\" and \"Day 2 Schedule\".\n\nAwards Gallery: A beautiful grid showcasing the specific awards: Champion, Runner-Up, Best Tactical Player, Best Endgame Player, Fastest Checkmate, Best Move, Best Beginner, and Audience Favourite.\n\nRules at a Glance: A clean, bulleted sidebar or footer area noting standard FIDE rules, no electronic devices, etc.\n\n3. Smooth Animations (Crucial):\n\nScroll Reveals: Sections and glassmorphism cards should fade in and slide up smoothly as the user scrolls down the page.\n\nHover Effects: Smooth, glowing border transitions when hovering over schedule items, award cards, or buttons.\n\nTab Switching: Switching between Day 1 and Day 2 schedules should have a fluid fade or slide animation, not a jarring instant cut.\n\nResponsive & Interactive: The webpage must look beautiful and adapt fluidly on both Desktop and Mobile devices. Stack grids cleanly on smaller screens.\n\nProvide the complete clean, modular code with all interactive UI mechanics (tabs, scrolling) and CSS animations working seamlessly out of the box. Start the workflow by rendering the main Hero layout and the Interactive Schedule. Do not build a playable game engine; this is strictly an event website.\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport fs from \'fs\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig, Plugin} from \'vite\';\n\n// LINT.IfChange(aistudio_media_plugin)\nfunction aistudioMediaPlugin(): Plugin {\n  return {\n    name: \'vite-plugin-aistudio-media\',\n    configureServer(server) {\n      server.middlewares.use((req, res, next) => {\n        if (req.url && req.url.startsWith(\'/assets/aistudio/\')) {\n          const rawPath = req.url.split(\'?\')[0].split(\'#\')[0];\n          try {\n            const decodedPath = decodeURIComponent(rawPath);\n            const relativePath = decodedPath.replace(/^\\//, \'\');\n            const aistudioDir = path.resolve(\n              __dirname,\n              \'public\',\n              \'assets\',\n              \'aistudio\',\n            );\n            const filePath = path.resolve(__dirname, \'public\', relativePath);\n            if (\n              filePath.startsWith(aistudioDir + path.sep) &&\n              fs.existsSync(filePath) &&\n              fs.statSync(filePath).isFile()\n            ) {\n              const ext = path.extname(filePath).toLowerCase();\n              const mimeMap: Record<string, string> = {\n                \'.jpg\': \'image/jpeg\',\n                \'.jpeg\': \'image/jpeg\',\n                \'.png\': \'image/png\',\n                \'.gif\': \'image/gif\',\n                \'.webp\': \'image/webp\',\n                \'.svg\': \'image/svg+xml\',\n                \'.bmp\': \'image/bmp\',\n                \'.ico\': \'image/x-icon\',\n                \'.mp4\': \'video/mp4\',\n                \'.webm\': \'video/webm\',\n                \'.ogv\': \'video/ogg\',\n                \'.mp3\': \'audio/mpeg\',\n                \'.wav\': \'audio/wav\',\n                \'.ogg\': \'audio/ogg\',\n                \'.pdf\': \'application/pdf\',\n              };\n              res.setHeader(\n                \'Content-Type\',\n                mimeMap[ext] || \'application/octet-stream\',\n              );\n              res.setHeader(\'Cache-Control\', \'no-cache\');\n              fs.createReadStream(filePath).pipe(res);\n              return;\n            }\n          } catch {\n            // Fall through if URI decoding or file access fails\n          }\n        }\n        next();\n      });\n    },\n  };\n}\n// LINT.ThenChange(//depot/google3/java/com/google/alkali/boq/makersuite/applet_dev_service/templates/initializers/react_theme/vite.config.ts:aistudio_media_plugin)\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss(), aistudioMediaPlugin()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    items {
      text: "User prompt: Act as an expert Full-Stack Developer and UI/UX Designer. Build a fully functional, highly modern, and animated Event Landing Page for a \"Chess eSports\" tournament.\n\nTech Stack: Use HTML, CSS, JavaScript (or React with Tailwind CSS depending on the tool capability).\n\nKey Requirements & Features:\n\n1. Modern Dark UI/UX Design (eSports Vibe):\n\nUse a sleek, premium dark mode aesthetic (Deep slate background #0f172a, with glowing accents like neon violet #8b5cf6 and gold #fbbf24 to match the flyer).\n\nUse crisp glassmorphism effects for content cards (schedules, rules, awards) rather than flat, boring boxes.\n\nTypography should be bold, modern, and highly legible, suited for a competitive gaming event.\n\n2. Core Website Sections (Based on the Event Flyer):\n\nHero Section: Big, bold title: \"CHESS eSPORTS: Compete. Think. Conquer.\" Display the key stats prominently: \"2 Days | 100 Players | 1 Champion\" alongside a glowing \"Register Now\" Call-to-Action button.\n\nAbout & eSports Experience: A grid section highlighting event features: Global Vibes, Live Boards, Live Commentary, and Audience Engagement. Use modern icons for each.\n\nTournament Overview & Format Details: A visual flowchart or clean step-layout showing the progression. Day 1 (100 Players -> Swiss System 5 Rounds -> Top 32 Qualify -> Round of 32). Day 2 (Round of 16 down to Grand Final). Include a small tooltip or text block explaining the Knockout rules (Best of 3, Best of 5, Blitz/Armageddon Tie-breaks).\n\nInteractive Schedule: An interactive Tab or Accordion component allowing the user to switch seamlessly between \"Day 1 Schedule\" and \"Day 2 Schedule\".\n\nAwards Gallery: A beautiful grid showcasing the specific awards: Champion, Runner-Up, Best Tactical Player, Best Endgame Player, Fastest Checkmate, Best Move, Best Beginner, and Audience Favourite.\n\nRules at a Glance: A clean, bulleted sidebar or footer area noting standard FIDE rules, no electronic devices