  planner_response {
    response: "I have updated the **Chess eSports** landing page to a **Shadowed Black and White** theme, while removing mock data and streamlining the layout.\n\n### Key Refinements\n\n- **Shadowed Black and White Aesthetic**: Replaced neon gradients and colors with a high-contrast monochrome design system featuring deep blacks (`#000000`, `zinc-950`), subtle borders (`zinc-800`), refined monospace telemetry accents, and crisp shadow elevations.\n- **Scrubbed Mock and Demo Data**: Removed placeholder competitor names, fake commentary feeds, and demo ratings, retaining only the authentic tournament structure, official time controls, stage progressions, and rule definitions.\n- **Minimalist Component Refactor**:\n  - **Navigation & Hero**: Clean typographic layout highlighting the core tagline (*\"Compete. Think. Conquer.\"*), verified metrics (*2 Days | 100 Players | 1 Champion*), and high-contrast call-to-action buttons.\n  - **Overview & Stages**: Streamlined stage breakdowns covering the 100-player Swiss qualifiers through the 16-player knockout championship.\n  - **Interactive Schedule**: Tabbed timeline for Day 1 and Day 2 with clear time stamps and status tags.\n  - **Awards & Recognition**: Minimalist podium and special category cards rendered in structured black-and-white panels.\n  - **Arena Telemetry**: Replaced flashy animated feeds with a clean DGT board telemetry console and arena production specifications.\n  - **Tactics Challenge & Rules**: Focused tactical puzzle and collapsible fair-play charter with strict arbiter guidelines.\n  - **Player Pass Registration**: Streamlined monochrome registration modal with digital player pass issuance and copyable pass IDs."
    modified_response: "I have updated the **Chess eSports** landing page to a **Shadowed Black and White** theme, while removing mock data and streamlining the layout.\n\n### Key Refinements\n\n- **Shadowed Black and White Aesthetic**: Replaced neon gradients and colors with a high-contrast monochrome design system featuring deep blacks (`#000000`, `zinc-950`), subtle borders (`zinc-800`), refined monospace telemetry accents, and crisp shadow elevations.\n- **Scrubbed Mock and Demo Data**: Removed placeholder competitor names, fake commentary feeds, and demo ratings, retaining only the authentic tournament structure, official time controls, stage progressions, and rule definitions.\n- **Minimalist Component Refactor**:\n  - **Navigation & Hero**: Clean typographic layout highlighting the core tagline (*\"Compete. Think. Conquer.\"*), verified metrics (*2 Days | 100 Players | 1 Champion*), and high-contrast call-to-action buttons.\n  - **Overview & Stages**: Streamlined stage breakdowns covering the 100-player Swiss qualifiers through the 16-player knockout championship.\n  - **Interactive Schedule**: Tabbed timeline for Day 1 and Day 2 with clear time stamps and status tags.\n  - **Awards & Recognition**: Minimalist podium and special category cards rendered in structured black-and-white panels.\n  - **Arena Telemetry**: Replaced flashy animated feeds with a clean DGT board telemetry console and arena production specifications.\n  - **Tactics Challenge & Rules**: Focused tactical puzzle and collapsible fair-play charter with strict arbiter guidelines.\n  - **Player Pass Registration**: Streamlined monochrome registration modal with digital player pass issuance and copyable pass IDs."
